  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-12), moved from the earlier photo",
  "mappingSource": "catalog turtlebeach.json from the EDCD EliteCustomButtonNames map 10F57055 (https://github.com/EDCD/EliteCustomButtonNames/tree/main/files/INTO%20Bindings/DeviceButtonMaps/10F57055.buttonMap) and apollomaniacs (https://www.apollomaniacs.com/flight_msfs_flightstick_en.htm): H1 = POV1, H2 = analog mini-stick Rx/Ry with click 19, B16/B17 = thumb plates",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The whole flightstick from the front right: the trigger (printed B18) faces the lower right, the base text (FLIGHTSTICK, TOGA, FLX MCT) reads from the upper left, so the pilot sits at the upper left and his left side is the photo's upper right (cyan-lit keys and lever), his right side the lower left (orange-lit keys and lever). Both key columns carry the same printed pairs (A = B1/B5 ... Y = B4/B8) and both levers TOGA = B9/B11, FULL REV = B10/B12; the catalog's left side = B1-B4 / B9-B10, right side = B5-B8 / B11-B12. TOGA is the forward end of the slots here (the catalog names it \"back\"). The head is seen from the front: the two hat caps behind the display are only edge-on and the B16/B17 plates behind them are hidden. The scroll wheel, slider and Xbox/View/Menu are not clearly identifiable (low candidates only).",
